// `#[group:]` describes a test and is read by nothing else, and a `#[group:]` written on a function is
// **accepted and ignored** - which is what every misplaced attribute in this language does today, not a rule
// of this one's. `todo/B24-orphan-attribute-is-silent.md` is that gap; this case is here so that closing it
// moves a golden rather than going unnoticed
#[group: "arithmetic"]
function helper() : int32
{
    return 1;
}

echo helper();
